{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "08", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "00", "M": "44", "S": "45"}}, "news": [{"title": "Larsen & Toubro to build Noida metro's Aqua Line extensions", "para": "Larsen & Toubro will initiate the construction of two new metro lines in Noida, aiming to improve access to Greater Noida and Jewar. One corridor will stretch from Botanical Garden to Sector 142 with eight elevated stations, complemented by an extension from Depot to Boraki connecting to a multimodal transport hub. Groundbreaking is expected to take place in the coming month.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/larsen-toubro-to-build-noida-metros-aqua-line-extensions/133025404?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-316852/133025404.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Every house in Chandigarh to be on waste map now", "para": "Chandigarh is finally extending segregated waste collection to ten densely populated residential pockets. These areas previously lacked formal waste collection, leading to open dumping and environmental concerns. The municipal corporation will deploy additional manpower and vehicles to cover these uncovered residential areas. This expansion aims to strengthen the city's faltering cleanliness drive and improve waste segregation compliance.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/every-house-in-chandigarh-to-be-on-waste-map-now/133025305?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-243298/133025305.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Three officials in Madurai suspended for unbuilt houses under PMAY-Gramin", "para": "Madurai revenue officers were suspended for siphoning housing scheme funds. They used photographs of existing houses to bypass mandatory GPS checks. This scheme aimed to provide housing for all citizens across India. An investigation revealed irregularities in nine of eighteen examined houses. Officials and residents colluded to divert Union government money.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/three-officials-in-madurai-suspended-for-unbuilt-houses-under-pmay-gramin/133025220?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-41004/133025220.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}